{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "YSU",
  "description": "The YSU (Yonsei University) nonlocal boundary-layer scheme of Hong, Noh and Dudhia (2006), with the stable-regime (Hong 2010) and top-down (theta_li) boundary-layer-top diagnostics of WRF 4.8, written as a single-column PDE component on the EarthSciDiscretizations grids/column_nonuniform_1d grid (layer index `lev`, layer 1 at the surface; interface index `lev_nodes`, interface 1 the surface). The physics is transcribed from the CCPP kernel bl_ysu_run in phys/physics_mmm/bl_ysu.F90 (NCAR/MMM-physics, the WRF 4.8 submodule). Prognostic column fields theta (potential temperature), u, v, qv, qc and qi obey the density-weighted flux-form vertical diffusion  d(c)/dt = (1/rho) d/dz[ rho K_c dc/dz - Phi_c ],  where K_c is the interface eddy diffusivity of the field (K_h for theta, K_m for u and v, K_q for water) and Phi_c is the prescribed (non-gradient) part of the turbulent flux: the surface flux on interface 1 (-hfx/cp for theta, -qfx for qv, rho_s u_*^2 u_1/|U| for momentum -- the sign convention of the ESD flux rule, Phi = rho K dc/dz on the face) and, inside the boundary layer, the YSU nonlocal (counter-gradient) flux rho K_c gamma_c plus the entrainment flux (w'c')_h ((z - z_1)/(h - z_1))^3, zero on the top interface. The gradient term is lowered by the ESD rule varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc applied to (rho K) on the interfaces (its own prescribed face fluxes kdudz_bot/kdudz_top are zero here because every prescribed flux is carried by Phi so that the six prognostic fields can share one rule instance), the prescribed-flux term by face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces. The density weighting is exactly the hydrostatic sigma-coordinate form of the Fortran: rho on an interface is (p[k] - p[k+1])/(g (zc[k+1] - zc[k])) and in a layer (p_int[k] - p_int[k+1])/(g dz[k]), so with WRF's pressures and heights the lowered operator reproduces bl_ysu_run's tridiagonal coefficients term by term (dsig xkzh rdz / del). Boundary-layer height: the bulk-Richardson search of components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/bulk_richardson.esm is applied (1) with the lowest-level theta_v, (2) with the thermal excess of the surface heat and moisture fluxes when the surface layer is unstable and the buoyancy flux positive, (3) the top-down theta_li scan that raises the top to just above the highest theta_li-unstable level (ysu_topdown_pblmix), and (4) the stable-regime search with the Hong (2010) critical value (0.25 over land, Rossby-number dependent over water) when the surface layer is stable and no boundary layer was found; each search is an aggregate over the level index and never a recurrence (see bulk_richardson.esm). Diffusivities: inside the boundary layer the K-profile K_m = k w_s z (1 - z/h)^p with the surface-layer velocity scale w_s = (u_*^3 + phifac k w_*^3 (1 - z/h))^(1/3) (or u_*/phi_m(z) when stable), K_h = K_m / Pr with the height-tapered Prandtl number of Hong et al. (2006, their eq. A10), K_q likewise; above the boundary layer the local Ri-dependent mixing-length diffusivity of Louis type with the in-cloud moist Richardson number; in the entrainment zone ((z - h)/delta)^2 < 4.6 the geometric mean of the local value and the entrainment-flux value -w_e dz_h exp(-((z - h)/delta)^2). Every diffusivity is floored by the background values and capped by xkzmax. Consumer-supplied inputs: the column fields (p, p_int, exner, ze and the initial theta, u, v, qv, qc, qi) are REWRITE-TARGET ops `input_<name>` (esm-spec 4.2 open tier) that the consumer lowers -- in the inline tests through a per-test `expression_template_imports` library (tests/scm_call<N>_inputs.esm, generated by tools/fill_tests.py from the instrumented WRF dumps) because esm-spec 6.6 `parameter_overrides` admit scalars only; surface-layer scalars (hfx, qfx, u_*, psi_m, psi_h, br, |U|, U10, land mask, z0, psfc) are ordinary parameters. NOT transcribed (the tests select regimes where the Fortran branches are inactive and assert that): the cloud-top radiative-driven entrainment branch (cloudflg: radsum, ent_eff, wstar3_2, hgamt2, wscalek2, the cloud-top zeroing of xkzm at kpbl-1) of ysu_topdown_pblmix, the BEP/BEP+BEM urban forcing terms, the optional ocean-current (uox/vox) surface drag, the topo_wind corrections (ctopo = ctopo2 = 1), the extra passive-tracer mixing (nmix = 0), and the WRF diagnostic outputs u10/v10 (pass-through), dusfc/dvsfc/dtsfc/dqsfc (column sums) and the TKE/hybrid-PBLH diagnostics. The cloud-top radiative-entrainment branch (ysu_topdown_pblmix, WRF cloudflg: a cloud layer at kpbl-1 whose integrated radiative cooling radsum drives top-down thermals wstar3_2, extra entrainment we_rad, a counter-gradient term hgamt2 and a second K-profile term wscalek2) is transcribed; radsum is the cumulative column integral of the radiative cooling. Tendencies are observed variables (`dthdt`, `dudt`, `dvdt`, `dqvdt`, `dqcdt`, `dqidt`) so that the inline tests assert the instantaneous right-hand side at time 0 against the real64 kernel's tendency extrapolated to dt -> 0 (Richardson extrapolation of the implicit step over dt = 0.04, 0.02, 0.01 s; the Fortran solves the diffusion implicitly, so its finite-step tendency differs from the derivative by O(dt K / dz^2)).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "atmospheric_dynamics",
   "boundary-layer",
   "pbl",
   "ysu",
   "wrf",
   "eddy-diffusivity",
   "column",
   "pde"
  ],
  "authors": [
   "EqWeFiC (WRF transcription)"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., Noh, Y., and Dudhia, J. (2006). A new vertical diffusion package with an explicit treatment of entrainment processes. Mon. Wea. Rev. 134, 2318-2341.",
    "doi": "10.1175/MWR3199.1"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Hong, S.-Y. (2010). A new stable boundary-layer mixing scheme and its impact on the simulated East Asian summer monsoon. Q. J. R. Meteorol. Soc. 136, 1481-1496.",
    "doi": "10.1002/qj.665"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and Pan, H.-L. (1996). Nonlocal boundary layer vertical diffusion in a medium-range forecast model. Mon. Wea. Rev. 124, 2322-2339.",
    "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(1996)124<2322:NBLVDI>2.0.CO;2"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Troen, I., and Mahrt, L. (1986). A simple model of the atmospheric boundary layer; sensitivity to surface evaporation. Boundary-Layer Meteorol. 37, 129-148.",
    "doi": "10.1007/BF00122760"
   },
   {
    "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_ysu.F90 (bl_ysu_run) at commit 550b5b4, the phys/physics_mmm submodule of WRF 4.8."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "YSU": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_from_bottom.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_thermo.esm"
    },
    {
     "ref": "./bulk_richardson.esm"
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    },
    "par": {
     "ref": "./ysu_parameters.esm"
    }
   },
   "expression_templates": {
    "above": {
     "params": [
      "f"
     ],
     "description": "Layer field f gathered at the layer just ABOVE interface kn (layer kn; clamped to NLEV so the top interface reads the top layer). Captures the enclosing aggregate's interface index `kn` by design.",
     "body": {
      "op": "index",
      "args": [
       "f",
       {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
         "kn",
         "NLEV"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    "below": {
     "params": [
      "f"
     ],
     "description": "Layer field f gathered at the layer just BELOW interface kn (layer kn-1; clamped to 1 so the surface interface reads layer 1). Captures the enclosing aggregate's interface index `kn` by design.",
     "body": {
      "op": "index",
      "args": [
       "f",
       {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "kn",
           1
          ]
         },
         1
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "theta": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Potential temperature (WRF thx)."
    },
    "u": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Zonal wind."
    },
    "v": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Meridional wind."
    },
    "qv": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Water-vapor mixing ratio."
    },
    "qc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio."
    },
    "qi": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Cloud-ice mixing ratio."
    },
    "rthraten": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Radiative potential-temperature tendency of the column (WRF rthraten), consumer-supplied through `input_rthraten`; read only by the cloud-top entrainment branch (radiative cooling of the cloud layer drives top-down thermals)."
    },
    "p": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer (half-level) pressure, consumer-supplied through the `input_p` rewrite target (WRF p2d)."
    },
    "p_int": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Interface (full-level) pressure, consumer-supplied through `input_p_int` (WRF p2di)."
    },
    "exner": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Exner function of the layer, consumer-supplied through `input_exner` (WRF pi2d)."
    },
    "ze": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Interface heights above ground, ze[1] = 0, consumer-supplied through `input_ze` (WRF zq, the cumulative sum of dz8w); the grid's single geometry input."
    },
    "zc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer mid-point heights (WRF za), grid-derived from ze."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer thicknesses (WRF dzq), grid-derived from ze; the finite-volume measure read by the rules."
    },
    "dzc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Centre-to-centre distance across interface kn, zc[kn] - zc[kn-1] (WRF dza(k+1)); zero on the two domain faces."
    },
    "rho_n": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Hydrostatic air density on interface kn, (p[kn-1] - p[kn]) / (g dzc[kn]); zero on the two domain faces, where no diffusive flux is computed."
    },
    "rho_c": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Hydrostatic air density of layer k, (p_int[k] - p_int[k+1]) / (g dz[k]) (WRF del/(g dzq))."
    },
    "T": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Absolute temperature theta exner (WRF tx)."
    },
    "thv": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Virtual potential temperature (WRF thvx)."
    },
    "thli": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Liquid-ice potential temperature (WRF thlix), used by the top-down boundary-layer-top scan."
    },
    "spd2": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Squared wind speed floored by spd2_min (WRF spdk2)."
    },
    "psfc": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "Pa",
     "default": 100000.0,
     "description": "Surface pressure (WRF psfcpa)."
    },
    "hfx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 100.0,
     "description": "Upward surface sensible-heat flux."
    },
    "qfx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
     "default": 5e-05,
     "description": "Upward surface moisture flux."
    },
    "ust": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.3,
     "description": "Friction velocity u_* from the surface-layer scheme."
    },
    "psim": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Integrated similarity function for momentum at the lowest level (WRF psim, used as fm = ln(z/z0) - psi_m)."
    },
    "psih": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Integrated similarity function for heat at the lowest level (WRF psih, fh)."
    },
    "br": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": -0.05,
     "description": "Surface-layer bulk Richardson number from the surface-layer scheme; br > 0 marks a stable surface layer (sfcflg = false)."
    },
    "wspd": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 5.0,
     "description": "Lowest-level wind speed of the surface-layer scheme (includes its convective-velocity enhancement), used in the surface drag and in gamma_u."
    },
    "u10": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 3.0,
     "description": "10-m zonal wind, used only in the over-water Rossby number of the stable critical bulk Richardson number."
    },
    "v10": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "10-m meridional wind (see u10)."
    },
    "xland": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "WRF land mask: 1 land, 2 water (xland >= 1.5 selects the over-water stable critical bulk Richardson number)."
    },
    "znt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.1,
     "description": "Roughness length z0 (see u10)."
    },
    "topdown": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "1 to enable the top-down theta_li boundary-layer-top scan (WRF namelist ysu_topdown_pblmix), 0 to disable."
    },
    "kdudz_bot": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "The ESD flux rule's prescribed surface value of rho K dc/dz. Zero: every prescribed surface flux enters through the Phi arrays instead, so that one rule instance serves all six prognostic fields. Declared without units on purpose: the rule subtracts this one name inside every field's flux row, so it must be unit-polymorphic (a units-free variable is dimension-agnostic to the checker); with units it could satisfy only one of the six fields."
    },
    "kdudz_top": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "The ESD flux rule's prescribed top value of rho K dc/dz; zero (rigid lid), as in the Fortran. Units omitted for the same reason as kdudz_bot."
    },
    "theta1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Lowest-layer potential temperature."
    },
    "u1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Lowest-layer zonal wind."
    },
    "v1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Lowest-layer meridional wind."
    },
    "qv1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "description": "Lowest-layer vapor mixing ratio."
    },
    "T1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Lowest-layer temperature."
    },
    "thv1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Lowest-layer virtual potential temperature."
    },
    "thli1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Lowest-layer liquid-ice potential temperature."
    },
    "zc1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Height of the lowest layer mid-point (WRF zl1)."
    },
    "rho_sfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "Surface air density from psfc and the lowest-layer state (WRF rhox)."
    },
    "govrth": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/(s^2*K)",
     "description": "g / theta_1 (WRF govrth)."
    },
    "wspd1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Lowest-layer wind speed |U_1| + eps (WRF wspd1)."
    },
    "sflux": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K*m/s",
     "description": "Kinematic surface buoyancy flux hfx/(rho cp) + ep_1 theta_1 qfx/rho (WRF sflux)."
    },
    "sfcflg": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 when the surface layer is unstable or neutral (br <= 0), 0 when stable (WRF sfcflg)."
    },
    "Ri1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Bulk Richardson profile of the first-guess search (reference theta_v1, no thermal excess)."
    },
    "kpbl1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "First stable level of the first-guess search."
    },
    "brdn1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Ri_b just below the first-guess top."
    },
    "brup1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Ri_b at the first-guess top."
    },
    "hpbl1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "First-guess boundary-layer height (WRF hpbl before the thermal enhancement; it sets the similarity functions and w_*)."
    },
    "kpbl1a": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "First-guess top level after the `hpbl < ze[2] -> kpbl = 1` reset."
    },
    "pblflg1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 when the first-guess search found a boundary layer deeper than the first layer."
    },
    "zol1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Surface-layer stability parameter z/L = br fm^2/fh, bounded away from zero on the unstable/stable side of sfcflg (WRF zol1)."
    },
    "hol1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "h/L at the surface-layer top, zol1 hpbl1 sfcfrac / z_1 (WRF hol1)."
    },
    "phim": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Similarity function for momentum at the surface-layer top."
    },
    "phih": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Similarity function for heat at the surface-layer top."
    },
    "bfx0": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K*m/s",
     "description": "Positive part of the surface buoyancy flux."
    },
    "wstar3": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s^3",
     "description": "Cube of the convective velocity scale g/theta_1 (w'theta_v')_s hpbl1 (zero when the surface layer is stable)."
    },
    "wstar": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Convective velocity scale w_* (WRF output wstar)."
    },
    "ust3": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s^3",
     "description": "u_*^3."
    },
    "wscale": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Bulk mixed-layer velocity scale w_s at z/h = 1/2 from the surface convective scale, (u_*^3 + phifac k w_*^3 zhalf)^(1/3) bounded by [u_*/aphi5, aphi16 u_*] (WRF wscale before the cloud-top branch); it sets the thermal excess of the boundary-layer-height search."
    },
    "wscale_c": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Mixed-layer velocity scale after the cloud-top branch: (u_*^3 + phifac k (w_*^3 + wstar3_2) zhalf)^(1/3) with the same bounds when cloudflg, else wscale (WRF wscale recomputed in the branch). It feeds the counter-gradient terms and the momentum counter-gradient factor, which the Fortran evaluates after the height diagnosis."
    },
    "convective": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 when the surface layer is unstable and the buoyancy flux positive: the nonlocal (counter-gradient, thermal-excess) terms are active."
    },
    "gamfac": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2*s/kg",
     "description": "b / (rho_s w_s) (WRF gamfac)."
    },
    "hgamt0": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Counter-gradient heat term before the positivity clip, min(gamfac hfx/cp, gamcrt)."
    },
    "hgamt0_c": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Counter-gradient heat term of the cloud-top branch's surface part, min(bfac hfx/(rho_s wscale_c c_p), gamcrt) (WRF hgamt recomputed with the branch's wscale)."
    },
    "hgamq0": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "description": "Counter-gradient moisture term before the positivity clip, min(gamfac qfx, gamcrq)."
    },
    "vpert": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Virtual thermal excess of the surface layer, a (hgamt0 + ep_1 theta_1 hgamq0) / b."
    },
    "excess": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Thermal excess added to the reference theta_v of the enhanced search, max(vpert, 0) min(z_1/(sfcfrac hpbl1), 1), zero unless convective."
    },
    "thermal": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Reference virtual potential temperature of the enhanced search, theta_v1 + excess (WRF thermal)."
    },
    "thermalli": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Reference liquid-ice potential temperature of the top-down scan, theta_li1 + excess (WRF thermalli)."
    },
    "hgamt": {
